  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q10",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "In the expansion of $\\left(3x+\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^n$, the constant term is 216. Find $n$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$n=4$.\n\nThe constant term occurs when equal numbers of $3x$ and $\\frac{2}{x}$ factors are selected.",
      "worked": "The general term is\n$$\\begin{align*}T_{k+1}&=\\binom{n}{k}(3x)^{n-k}\\left(\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^k\\\\T_{k+1}&=\\binom{n}{k}3^{n-k}2^k x^{n-2k}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor a constant term, $n-2k=0$, so $n=2k$. Its value is $\\binom{2k}{k}6^k$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{2}{1}6^1&=12,\\\\\\binom{4}{2}6^2&=6\\times36,\\\\\\binom{4}{2}6^2&=216.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $k=2$ and $n=4$. The values $\\binom{2k}{k}6^k$ increase with positive integer $k$, so this is the only solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
  },
